  <static seed="1911" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/NumberBasics/AbsoluteValue10.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ |{2}|= }</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The absolute value of <m>2</m> is the distance between <m>2</m> and <m>0</m> on the number line. In this case, since <m>2</m> is <m>2</m> units away from 0, the answer is <m>2</m>.</p>
</solution>
